        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "@6H075T2, after some recent changes, I *think* adding space padding to title now should be possible. You can follow the [newly added example](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/974ebc04dff3b59899a5eee29157a9bbfd85dce3/doc/mini-files.txt#L393-L411) (without the `config.height` part) and it should work.\r\n\r\nThis use case even has a [dedicated test](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/974ebc04dff3b59899a5eee29157a9bbfd85dce3/tests/test_files.lua#L3870-L3877) in the hope that it will keep working.\r\n\r\nI changed my mind about this issue because height also could not be customized (see #1140). As the root cause has revealed to be the same (intentional blocking of too frequent `MiniFilesWindowUpdate` event triggering), it seems to be more reasonable to change the balance here (from preferring performance to preferring actual customization with [heavy warning that it is triggered frequently](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/974ebc04dff3b59899a5eee29157a9bbfd85dce3/doc/mini-files.txt#L330).",
