        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> This only happens when a floating window has a long directory title, becomes contracted and unfocused makes the padding on the right gone and not consistent with the left padding as it doesn't appends an empty space in the end.\r\n\r\nThat's expected because width of windows are fixed and can be configured [inside `config.windows`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3eb07050b25520a4ca011473a3f5dbf56273cb9d/doc/mini-files.txt#L602-L607). So it looks like just a coincidence of the title length being strictly on character less than window width.",
            "created_at": "2024-09-10T12:56:39Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1062#issuecomment-2340674951",
